	TODO:
	- check the chords (real book).
	- check the tune (real book).
	- hear the tune to check that it is right and adjust the tempo.
	- the intro/vamp figure (bars 1-4 and the end of the A section) is written on the bottom line of the staff (E) in this book; the transposed (Bb) real book seems to write it one step lower (concert D). Check against a recording.
	- the page shows no key signature (only the time signature); it is written here in D minor (one flat), as the B flats under G-7, A7b9 and E-7b5 B flat7 imply and as the transposed (Bb) real book has it.
	- bar 9 (G-7): the first four eighths are hard to read (written here as A G F# G), and the B flat pair is written here as a dotted eighth and a sixteenth. Check them.
	REMARKS:
	- the real book prints 'Varmland' where the composer usually goes: this is the traditional Swedish song 'Ack Varmeland, du skona'.
	- the real book prints no style word for this tune, so there is no piece attribute.
	- form as printed: a four bar intro vamp with a repeat sign, then a repeated A section (with the segno) ending with the vamp, then the B section with 'D.S. al Coda'. The coda sign is printed at bar 10 (the second D- bar of A).
	- the third and fourth bars of the intro (and of the vamp, and the fourth and fifth bars of the coda) are a two bar repeat sign in the book; they are written out here.
	- the A7 alt chord of the coda is written here as A7#5#9.
	- the two last bars of the coda are rests (D-).
